{"title":"Data and conditions","partialurl":"data","pagetemplateid":"b4700000-0000-4000-8000-2546863c3d7d","publishingstateid":"b4700000-0000-4000-8000-73c49e548d0c","hiddenfromsitemap":false,"sharedpageconfiguration":false,"displayorder":3.1,"isroot":false,"rootwebpageid":"b4800000-0000-4000-8000-000000000031","parentpageid":"b4800000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","copy":"<div class="demo" data-liquid-page="data"><p class="demo-kicker">Liquid / data</p><h1>Turn records into a useful page.</h1><p class="demo-lead">Apply a small, explicit server-side filter. FetchXML returns account records; Liquid assigns values, branches on status and passes each record to a reusable card.</p>{% include 'Liquid navigation' active:'data' %}{{ snippets['Demo/Liquid guidance'] }}{% if user %}{% include 'Liquid data results' %}{% else %}<section class="demo-panel"><h2>Sign in to load account records</h2><p>Liquid data queries honor the current portal identity and table permissions.</p><a class="demo-button" href="/SignIn?returnUrl=%2Fliquid%2Fdata%2F">Choose your identity</a></section>{% endif %}<section class="demo-panel"><h2>Follow the transformation</h2><ol><li><code>assign</code> accepts Active, All or Inactive; unknown input defaults to Active.</li><li><code>unless</code> and <code>if</code> emit a state filter in bounded FetchXML.</li><li><code>capture</code> constructs the visible result summary.</li><li><code>for</code> passes each account, index and status into the card partial.</li></ol><pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;padding:20px;background:var(--demo-paper);border:1px solid var(--demo-border);border-radius:4px"><code>{% raw %}{% capture result_summary %}
  {{ account_query.results.entities.size }} {{ chosen_status }} accounts
{% endcapture %}
{% for account_record in account_query.results.entities %}
  {% include 'Liquid account card' record:account_record index:forloop.index %}
{% endfor %}{% endraw %}</code></pre><p>These reads do not issue browser Web API calls. Check the query and include chain in Inspect, then edit the source and compare local rendering with your deployed portal.</p></section></div>
","customcss":""}
